      "assessment": "R1 G4 keeps the original paired direction correctly and recognises the combined mid-window edit cannot identify which component caused its -0.020347 Mean. The two one-component reversals are appropriate. The narrative abbreviates a Q3 loss plus Q4 loss as a single upper-quartile loss, and calls zero clipping evidence of not saturation but does not confuse it with benefit.",
      "decision_update": "[5,5,6,5] is selected as R2 G4; [5,4,5,5] is unselected. This isolates one schedule component relative to the observed source array, subject to the common next-parent change. Retain component-reversal proposals as an evidence-generating alternative to automatic escalation.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "Only latest endpoint geometry at75 was fetched; no matched control or candidate-level trace supports structural causality. One selected reversal alone does not establish additivity or rule out interaction with the unselected component.",
