    {
      "id": "v2/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top2/r01/synthesis",
      "evidence_sha256": "6f4acafe730222c5099f4fd48f1da75ac088b08b3b211c480cdac46f396946b7",
      "assessment": "R1 synthesis correctly restores the G1 Best increase (+0.080) missed by its private analyst, compares all six same-wave pairs and treats shared parents as dependent. It selects a useful mix of early continuation, conditional additions and mid-component reversal. Nevertheless it invents numeric response bands (0.005, 0.02) and requires median/win-rate improvement before extending concentrated Mean gains, contrary to the primary objective.",
      "decision_update": "R2 selected arrays [6,5,5,6], [6,6,5,5], [7,5,5,5], [5,5,6,5] all execute. These test beyond the initial local bracket, unlike Top1 stagnation. Forecasts based on adding R0 effects should be labelled conditional hypotheses, not bounded-downside estimates; later measured marginal response must update them.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The synthesis acknowledges parent change and unmeasured interaction, but uses additivity in ranking and causal exclusion. R0 pair median retains a reciprocal sign error. No evidence supports a universal plateau threshold or treating a few real, valid contributors as an invalid Mean gain.",
