    {
      "id": "v2/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top2/r02/G2",
      "evidence_sha256": "dab18474c33a92a1634e53fd17c019ad79da03655ab2ba39b63aba6f96ab2509",
      "assessment": "R2 G2 retrieves the actual r01-to-latest pair and interval delivery, showing a small +0.000077 increment with 50% wins despite increased interval1 motion. It correctly drops unsupported stacking. However candidate contributions are miscalculated: 3.535/100 and 3.230/100 are about 0.0354 and 0.0323, not 0.065 and 0.060; a maximum incumbent contribution 0.007 cannot explain its entire 0.031 gap.",
      "decision_update": "Its [6,5,6,5] is selected for R3 G2; [7,5,5,5] is rejected as already executed and harmful in the current peer. This supports council-level deduplication and provenance, while private proposals may legitimately lack current peer outcomes. Avoid claiming any later window permanently inert from a single conditional null.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "It says no noise band is known but introduces a 0.001 null band in the falsifier. It also says motion falls monotonically although it rises in the last window. Neither concentration nor tiny median removes valid Mean contributions.",
