      "evidence_sha256": "d0b3b519954298671f3fa1c6e8f39eb5bd204b8a8631bc814d2ea49b18f31ffe",
      "assessment": "R2 G3 observes the intended monotonicity test fail: early 6-to-7 loses 0.063475 with upper-stratum losses while delivered motion increases. It appropriately proposes a one-tick reversal and a conditional mid-window probe instead of escalation. Nevertheless it calls its latest fixed group the actual pre-round parent, despite the common mixed-TOP1 parent policy, and overstates a local interior optimum from parent-confounded comparisons.",
      "decision_update": "Both proposals execute in R3: [6,5,5,5] as G1 and [7,5,6,5] as G4. The reversal explicitly acknowledges an existing schedule under a new parent; this is a useful purposeful repeat. The mid addition tests conditional interaction rather than merely repeating the losing early dose.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "No matched r01 geometry was obtained, and large absolute early RMS does not make geometry intrinsically unusable. Best actually drops from 7.78846 to 7.70807; one proposal sentence says tick7 preserved it. Findings support a local tested loss, not a universal amplitude optimum.",
